  "body": "Found in the review read of PR #3625 (#3362). **This is a hypothesis from a read of the code. No test or run shows it yet. The first step is a test.** The priority is `P1` because the possible result is a gouge that passes; correct the priority when the test gives the answer.\n\n## What the read found\n\n`emit_runs` in `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/march.rs` (about lines 347-390 on `main` at `7c637d705`), the plain hop between two runs (about lines 381-383): the travel height is `trav = hop.max(z0)`, where `hop` is the retract height and `z0` is the Z of the start of the next run. The Z of the end of the current run (`cur.z`) is not in the formula. The hop is not checked against the model.\n\nIf the run that ends is higher than the start of the next run, and the retract height is below `cur.z`, the tool moves down at the current XY to `trav`, and then makes a rapid across at that height. At the current XY the tool is on the surface. A move down from there goes into the part.\n\n## Where it can occur\n\n- On `main` today: a cavity with the Contour or Flat pattern (the outer pass is high, the inner pass is low), when the retract height of the operation is below the high pass.\n- With PR #3625 and `Pass starts at: Inside`: a convex part (a dome), because the inner pass is high and the next pass is lower.\n- With a retract height above the top of the part (the usual setup) the fault cannot occur: `hop` is then above `cur.z`.\n\n## Not known\n\n1. Whether a rule refuses a retract height below the top of the part when the operation is made or edited.\n2. Whether the verifier gives a blocking finding for the move down and for the rapid across.\n\n## Wanted\n\n1. A test, first: a cavity fixture on `main` with Contour, a retract height between the two passes, and the verifier. Read the moves of the hop, and the findings.\n2. If the tool goes into the part: `trav` must not be below `cur.z` (for example `hop.max(z0).max(cur.z)`), and the rapid across must be checked like the other links (`diagonal_ok` / `straight_ok`) or go to the clearance height. Pin it for a cavity and for a dome.\n3. If a rule already refuses that retract height, or the verifier blocks the post: say so here, pin that fact, and set the priority to `P3` or close the issue with the pin.\n\nThe decision file of PR #3625 says that each link \"is certified by the existing laws\". Correct that sentence for the plain hop when the answer is known.\n",
